<title>USA: US House majority leader plans flat tax bill.</title>
<headline>US House majority leader plans flat tax bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Majority Leader Dick Armey this week will introduce a bill that would replace the current income tax with a flat 17 percent rate on all income, a spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Armey, a Texas Republican, and Sen. Richard Shelby, an Alabama Republican, will hold a media briefing to discuss the bill Wednesday.</p>
